 "notes": [
  {
   "id": "vn-symmetric-exchange-develop-the-side-you-intend-to-castle-into",
   "line": "e4 Nf6 Nc3 d5 exd5 Nxd5 Nxd5 Qxd5 Nf3 Bg4",
   "teaches": "Decide which way the king is going BEFORE choosing developing squares, then bring out the pieces on that wing first — castling long is only fast if the queenside is already clear, and each developing move should also ask a question.",
   "explains": "The bishop comes to g4 onto the knight on f3, which both develops toward the queenside plan and provokes a reply. The other queenside piece follows next move, and the king goes long behind them. A bishop that pins on its way out buys the tempo that makes the plan work.",
